 the regex might still be at the last match position after the `exec` loop. Let me reset it or use a fresh regex for the replace.\n\nBetter approach: create a new regex for the replace:\n```typescript\ncontent = content.replace(/^\\[\\^(\\d+)\\]:\\s*(.*)$/gm, '');\n```\n\nYeah, using a fresh regex literal for the replace avoids the `lastIndex` issue.\n\nThen for references:\n```typescript\ncontent = content.replace(/\\[\\^(\\d+)\\]/g, (_, num) => {\n  const fn = footnotes.find(f => f.num === num);\n  if (fn) {\n    return `<sup><a href=\"#fn-${fn.num}\">${fn.num}</a></sup>`;\n  }\n  return _;\n});\n```\n\nThis should work. Let me now write all the code.\n\nOK, I'm going to create all 8 plugin files now, plus the index.ts for plugins. Let me write them simultaneously.","signature":"eb61f640-46ca-4ecd-ba41-651dedc8a101"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":38912,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b50c0f90-70ef-40a6-86b6-71377e12f620","uuid":"a6060cb3-a8eb-499f-98b0-6ac0f421f137"}
